course: dictionary
lesson: 6122
title: The middle of things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word middle means the part halfway between two ends or sides. In a row of three, the middle one is the second. When you meet middle in a text, look at the words around it to find which kind of middle the writer means.
explain: Middle can also be about time. «In the middle of the night» means the part of the night between its start and its end. The clue is the word night, which tells you it is a time, not a place.
explain: «Most of the middle of Australia, called the Outback, is hot and dry.» Here the middle is the central part of a place, far from the edges. You can check by swapping in centre: the centre of Australia is also hot and dry, so your meaning fits.
fact: The middle is the part halfway between the two ends or sides.
fact: «The middle of the night» means the part of time between its start and end.
fact: As an adjective, middle means in the centre, as in «the middle child».
fact: «In the middle of doing something» means busy doing it right now.
fact: In «an atom», the nucleus is its tiny middle, with electrons around it.
exercise: «Most of the middle of Australia, called the Outback, is hot and dry.» In this sentence, what does middle mean? | The coast, where the sea is | *The central part, far from the edges | The very end of the country | The wettest part
exercise: In a row of three, which one is the middle? | The third | *The second | The first | The last
exercise: «In the middle of doing something» means what? | Starting fresh tomorrow | Finished and tidy | *Busy doing it right now | Lost in a crowd
test: «The Okavango river floods in the middle of the dry season.» What does middle mean here? | The end of the rainy season | *The part of the season between its start and end | The coldest day of the year | The very start of the dry season
test: A story has a beginning, a middle and an end. Which part comes between the beginning and the end? | The last page | The start | The title | *The middle
exam: Which phrase means the part of time between its start and end? | *the middle of the night | the middle finger | the middle child | a middle name
